11-13T18:10:00Z","closed_at":"2025-11-13T18:09:56Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nReproducible in v4.6.dev3.official [9d84f3d13]\n\n### System information\n\nWindows 11 - Godot Engine v4.6.dev3.official.9d84f3d13 - Vulkan 1.3.280 - Forward+ - Using Device #0: NVIDIA - NVIDIA GeForce RTX 3070\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhenever you create a node and attach a script to it for the first time, and then run the game and go to the \"remote\" tab, the console throws an error related to the script. This happens the first time. After that, you can detach and attach the script or a new one without the error occurring. It only happens if you add a new node with a different name (I say this because if you delete the existing node and add a new one with the same name as the previous one, the error doesn't occur. It only happens with a new node and a name that has never existed in the node tree).\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/73457ade-2d9b-4076-b1bb-173c850bca82\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nCreate a new project. Create the main scene. Create a new node, for example, Node3D. Attach a script to this new node. Run the game and open the \"REMOTE\" tab.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[error-project.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/23531961/error-project.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_u